# RPATH for CEF's private ANGLE libraries is intentional and Debian-compliant.
#
# CEF requires specific ANGLE libraries (libEGL.so, libGLESv2.so) which are
# Google's OpenGL ES implementation, NOT Mesa. These conflict with system
# libegl1/libgles2 packages, so they're installed to /usr/lib/x86_64-linux-gnu/cef/
#
# According to Debian policy (https://wiki.debian.org/RpathIssue):
# "The only time a binary or shared library in a Debian package should set
# RPATH or RUNPATH is if it is linked to private shared libraries in the
# same package. In that case, place those private shared libraries in
# /usr/lib/<package>."
#
# The ANGLE libraries are private to CEF and installed in /usr/lib/.../cef/,
# which follows this guideline. The RPATH allows CEF to find them at runtime
# without requiring users to set LD_LIBRARY_PATH.
# Suppress the RPATH warning for libcef.so - it needs to find private ANGLE libraries
libcef138: custom-library-search-path RUNPATH /usr/lib/x86_64-linux-gnu/cef [usr/lib/x86_64-linux-gnu/libcef.so.138.0.1]
